      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #34118.\n\nThe \"Add the Model to the Test Suite\" section of [Support New Models](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/supported-models/support_new_models#add-the-model-to-the-test-suite) no longer matches the repository:\n\n- The `test_generation_models.py` link points to `test/registered/models/`, which returns a 404. The file now lives at `test/registered/e2e/models/test_generation_models.py`.\n- The doc says to add the model to `ALL_OTHER_MODELS`, but the test file now uses a single `ALL_MODELS` list.\n- The example command runs `TestGenerationModels.test_others`, which no longer exists. The current test method is `test_all_models`. The command also only works from the test's directory, which the doc didn't mention.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDocs only: `docs/docs/supported-models/support_new_models.mdx`\n\n1. Updated the link to `https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/test/registered/e2e/models/test_generation_models.py`.\n2. Renamed `ALL_OTHER_MODELS` to `ALL_MODELS`.\n3. Updated the example command to:\n   ```bash\n   cd test/registered/e2e/models\n   ONLY_RUN=Qwen/Qwen2-1.5B python3 -m unittest test_generation_models.TestGenerationModels.test_all_models\n   ```\n\nI checked each change against current `main`: the new link returns 200, `ALL_MODELS` is defined in the test file, `TestGenerationModels.test_all_models` exists, and `ONLY_RUN` is still how the test filters by model.\n\nNote: #34156 and #40400 also change this link, but neither updates the list name or the command. This PR covers all three. (#34156 also points to `test/registered/models_e2e/`, which doesn't exist on current `main`.)\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A (docs-only change).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (docs-only change).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (N/A, docs only)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (N/A, docs only)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39921677161](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39921677161)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39921677127](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39921677127)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
